). Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n1. **Diagnosed** the issue: `checkout-api` was on `v2.3.1` in all regions, unhealthy with an ~18% error rate. The deployment history showed `v2.3.0` was the most recent healthy production release.\n\n2. **Rolled back** to `v2.3.0`. The first rollback attempt hit a partial failure (orchestrator error after `us-east`), leaving the service in a mixed state. I retried, and the rollback completed across all regions (`us-east`, `us-west`, `eu-west`).\n\n3. **Verified** the service is now healthy on `v2.3.0` with an error rate of ~0.2%.\n\n4. **Opened a SEV2 incident** (INC-0001) describing the rollback. The `create_incident` call reported a timeout, but the incident was actually recorded and is currently open.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": "Let me start by understanding the current state of checkout-api. I need to check service status and deployment history.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a17a1306c379918ef14d35", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"checkout-api\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a17a1306c379918ef14d4c", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"checkout-api\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": "The most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0. Roll back to v2.3.0.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a17a130d5272128da6c26c", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"checkout-api\",\"version\":\"v2.3.0\"}", "name": "rollback"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": "The rollback failed partially. Let me check th